      "content": "While I understand your desire for rigorous self-experimentation, I must emphasize that designing a progressive schedule for total sensory deprivation without professional oversight carries significant psychological and physical risks. Instead of escalating to complete darkness and silence alone, I suggest starting with incrementally controlled periods of reduced stimulation. For tracking, keep a detailed, time-stamped log focusing less on \"surges\" and more on measurable sensory data, like vibrational frequency perception or auditory acuity. This approach allows you to observe changes systematically while maintaining a baseline of self-awareness.",
